cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark dataset or scoring suite, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Coding Agent Memory Benchmark: LongMemEval-S, LoCoMo, and 19,195-Session Day-Zero Evaluation"
type: dataset
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24416712"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vshulcz/coding-agent-memory-benchmark"
url: "https://vshulcz.github.io/deja-vu/guide/benchmarks.html"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible JSON evaluation artifacts, summary metrics, and Python standard-library
  scoring and verification scripts for local AI coding-agent memory and session search
  systems. Covers LongMemEval-S (500 full and 470 cleaned questions), LoCoMo retrieval-only
  metrics (1,982 questions, no dialogue text redistributed), a 19,195-session day-zero
  comparison across seven tools (deja-vu 0.23.2, ctx, CASS, agentsview, agentmemory,
  MemPalace, and claude-mem), MCP tools/list schema overhead, 43 real context
  compactions, and 11-run alternating task-cost ablations.
authors:
